.TH AME 1 "2026-10-27" "ame" "functorOS fleet tools"
.SH NAME
ame \- build, deploy and track NixOS generations across the functorOS fleet
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ame
.I command
.RI [ args .\|.\|.]
.PP
.B ame
.RB { build | switch | boot | test | update }
.RI [ host .\|.\|.]
.br
.B ame fetch
.RI [ generation ]
.br
.B ame record
.RI [ generation ]
.br
.B ame digest
.RI [ generation ]
.br
.B ame check
.RB { current | gen | cache | flake | all }
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B ame
drives the flake at
.I ~/.config/ame
for every machine in the fleet.
It has two halves.
.PP
The
.B build
half runs on
.BR shirakami-fubuki ,
which is the only machine with the CPU and the emulation set up to build the
whole fleet. It builds each host's system closure locally and then activates it
\(em on this machine directly, on the others over SSH across the tailnet.
A host that is offline is still built, and the result is kept as a GC root under
.IR $XDG_CACHE_HOME/ame ,
so the next run only has to copy it.
.PP
The
.B generation
half is for the receiving machines.
.B shirakami-fubuki
publishes its store over
.BR harmonia (1)
as a signed binary cache; the monthly builder records each completed fleet build
as a numbered
.IR generation .
On
.B nanashi
or
.BR kanade ,
.B ame fetch
pulls that generation's closure out of the cache instead of rebuilding it.
.SS Generations
A generation is one line of JSON in
.IR $XDG_CACHE_HOME/ame/generations.jsonl ,
appended only after
.I every
host in it built successfully. It records the generation label (by default
.BR YYYY-MM ),
the build timestamp, the flake's git revision, a short hash of
.IR flake.lock ,
the store path per host, and the path of that generation's update digest.
.PP
Because a generation is appended atomically at the end,
.B ame fetch latest
can never land on a half-built set.
.SH COMMANDS
.SS Build and deploy
.TP
.BI build " [host...]"
Build only. Nothing is activated and no machine is touched.
.TP
.BI switch " [host...]"
Build, then activate immediately. Other hosts are done first and this one last,
so a network hiccup during its own activation cannot cut off a deploy still in
flight.
.TP
.BI boot " [host...]"
Build, then make it the default for the next boot without changing what is
running.
.TP
.BI test " [host...]"
Build, then activate without making it the boot default.
.TP
.BI update " [host...]"
Run
.B nix flake update
first, then build.
.PP
With no host arguments every host is targeted. An unknown host name is an error
rather than a no-op.
.SS Generations
.TP
.BI fetch " [generation]"
Fetch the closure recorded for
.I this
host in
.I generation
(default:
.BR latest )
from the binary cache, and register a GC root for it under
.IR $XDG_CACHE_HOME/ame/fetched/ .
.IP
.B This does not activate anything.
Activation needs root, and
.B ame
deliberately does not escalate. The command prints the exact
.B switch-to-configuration
invocation to run.
.IP
Fails if the generation has no build for this host, naming the hosts it does
have.
.TP
.BI record " [generation]"
Append the closures currently linked under
.I $XDG_CACHE_HOME/ame
as a new generation (default label:
.BR YYYY-MM ).
Refuses if any host in the fleet has no build. Normally called by the monthly
builder; run it by hand to seed the registry.
.TP
.BI digest " [generation]"
Print the update digest written for that generation \(em what moved, and what
looks like it could break. Default:
.BR latest .
.SS Status
.TP
.B check current
What this host is running: store path, NixOS version and label, build date, and
the running kernel against the one in the closure (they differ after a
.B switch
without a reboot, which is the most common cause of "the fix did not work").
Also names which recorded generation the running closure came from, if any, and
says so when a newer one is available.
.TP
.B check gen
List every recorded generation with its build date, flake revision, and the
hosts it covers.
.TP
.B check cache
Whether the binary cache answers. On failure, points at
.B systemctl status harmonia
on the builder.
.TP
.B check flake
Git state of the flake checkout: branch, unpushed and unpulled commit counts,
and how many paths are uncommitted. Fetches from
.B origin
first, and reports local state only if that fails.
.TP
.B check all
All four, in order.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B AME_FLAKE
Override the flake location. Defaults to the path baked in at build time
.RI ( config.functorOS.flakeLocation ).
.TP
.B XDG_CACHE_HOME
Where build out-links, the generation registry and fetched GC roots live.
Defaults to
.IR ~/.cache .
.TP
.B NIX_SSHOPTS
Set by
.B ame
itself for its SSH calls
.RB ( BatchMode=yes ,
.BR ConnectTimeout=10 ,
.BR StrictHostKeyChecking=accept-new ).
Overriding it is not recommended.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/ame
The flake.
.TP
.I $XDG_CACHE_HOME/ame/<host>
Build out-link per host. Doubles as a GC root.
.TP
.I $XDG_CACHE_HOME/ame/generations.jsonl
The generation registry, one JSON object per line, newest last.
.TP
.I $XDG_CACHE_HOME/ame/generations/<gen>.md
Update digest for that generation.
.TP
.I $XDG_CACHE_HOME/ame/fetched/<gen>
GC root for a fetched-but-not-activated generation.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
A build, activation, or fetch failed.
.TP
.B 2
Usage error \(em unknown command or unknown host.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Build everything without touching any machine:
.PP
.RS
.nf
ame build
.fi
.RE
.PP
Deploy to one host:
.PP
.RS
.nf
ame switch nanashi
.fi
.RE
.PP
On a laptop, take the newest published generation and activate it:
.PP
.RS
.nf
ame fetch latest
sudo /nix/store/...-nixos-system-.../bin/switch-to-configuration switch
.fi
.RE
.PP
Pin to a specific month instead of the newest:
.PP
.RS
.nf
ame check gen
ame fetch 2026-11
.fi
.RE
.PP
Find out whether this machine is behind, and read what changed:
.PP
.RS
.nf
ame check current
ame digest latest
.fi
.RE
.SH NOTES
.B ame
never escalates privileges on its own.
.BR switch ,
.B boot
and
.B test
use
.BR nixos-rebuild ,
which elevates via
.B run0
locally and logs in as
.B root
over SSH for remote hosts (see
.IR modules/deploy-target.nix );
.B fetch
does not activate at all and prints the root command for you to run.
.PP
The signing key for the cache is held only by
.BR shirakami-fubuki ,
as an agenix secret. The other hosts carry the public half in
.I nix.settings.trusted-public-keys
and so will refuse an unsigned or wrongly-signed path \(em which is the point.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR nixos-rebuild (8),
.BR nix (1),
.BR harmonia (1),
.BR agenix (1)
